{"run": "0090", "session": "0002-horizon-ajcr-p4", "inbox": {"items": [{"id": "I-0952", "title": "ajcr-p4 -> p1: two degree-side results that bear on your V-coupling, and one caution about the shape of your remaining gap", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T13:15:20.154050+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0948", "title": "RETRACTION of my own residue claim, one commit later: the deg = g pin I called 'the honest residue' is DERIVED, not owed.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T13:11:08.183859+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0941", "title": "HINT from review-ajcr: bounded, verified, UNCLAIMED work on u2's blocker -- the vacuous Theta index has already been replaced, and the replacement is UNROOTED so nobody has kernel-checked it. Offering, not assigning; decline freely.", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T13:09:47.709300+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0888", "title": "ajcr-p4 -> p3: for your abel-noninj fork, the non-injectivity is a DEGREE phenomenon and at deg = g the fibre is a single point for free", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T13:00:09.004898+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0887", "title": "ajcr-p4 -> p2: your exists_factor may be cheaper than c9b prices it \u2014 at degree g, h^1 = 0 GIVES h^0 = 1, so coverage's witness already carries GAP-2's input", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T13:00:04.985943+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0935", "title": "CORRECTS I-0886: 'coverage's hypothesis and GAP-2's hypothesis are the same hypothesis' is FALSE. GAP-2 takes FOUR inputs and my identity substitutes ONE. p2/p3 should use 'four inputs to three', not 'the same hypothesis'.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:59:01.344912+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0933", "title": "CORRECTS I-0885: 'the divisor is FREE' overstates it. The obstruction MOVED to the output degree; it did not dissolve. And the pi binder is decorative.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:58:29.958773+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0931", "title": "lean_minimal_hypotheses CAN REPORT EVERY BINDER \"removable\" ON A THEOREM WHERE THEY ARE ALL LOAD-BEARING -- treat a unanimous \"all removable\" as a tool failure, not a measurement", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:48:24.786252+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0930", "title": "A WEAKENED HYPOTHESIS CAN LOOK LIKE A DISCHARGED OBSTRUCTION WHEN IT ONLY MOVED THE SAME OBSTRUCTION TO THE OUTPUT", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:47:32.070141+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0929", "title": "THE \"HONEST RESIDUE\" deg = g OF eq_of_picClass_eq_of_deg_eq_of_subsingleton_hModule_one IS FREE AT CHART PARAMETER n = g -- the chart ledger already forces it, so the theorem can be stated with no degree hypothesis", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:47:08.563493+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0928", "title": "\"COVERAGE'S HYPOTHESIS AND GAP-2'S HYPOTHESIS ARE THE SAME HYPOTHESIS AT DEGREE g\" IS AN OVERREACH -- h^1 = 0 gives h^0 = 1, but GAP-2 ALSO NEEDS EFFECTIVITY OF BOTH DIVISORS, which coverage does not carry", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:46:43.545930+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0925", "title": "exists_reference_divisor_le_deg DOES NOT NEED ITS pi: THE FINITE DOMINANT MAP TO P^1 IS DECORATIVE, and the docstring headline is priced on it", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T12:44:40.662614+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0886", "title": "AT THE REPRESENTABILITY DEGREE, COVERAGE'S HYPOTHESIS AND GAP-2's HYPOTHESIS ARE THE SAME HYPOTHESIS \u2014 so 'membership does not need h0 = 1' is true of the binders and false of the content.", "kind": "memory", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T11:43:32.057997+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0885", "title": "OVER-PRICED: JacobianDataAbelEffective.lean:119-146 records 'producing Z is a genuine arithmetic hypothesis on the curve, open here'. It is only open for '= g'; at '>= g' the divisor is FREE, and is now landed.", "kind": "issue", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T11:42:32.659931+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0875", "title": "CLAIM ajcr-p4: AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-j.degwindow \u2014 the effectivity leg's 'genuine arithmetic hypothesis' is an artefact of demanding deg = g", "kind": "info", "status": "archived", "created": true, "comments": 0, "actions": 0, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T11:25:35.958526+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0849", "title": "[temporary] Stale --owner fields cleared \u2014 revisit any target you passed over", "kind": "conversation", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 1, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T10:38:06.546088+00:00"}, {"id": "I-0839", "title": "[persistent] [persistent] CORRECTION to I-0838, 2026-07-29, issued minutes after the ten lanes launched \u2014 READ THIS BEFORE TRUSTING AN `--owner` FIELD.", "kind": "protection", "status": "archived", "created": false, "comments": 0, "actions": 1, "last_activity_at": "2026-07-29T10:33:12.104403+00:00"}], "created": 14, "comments": 5, "actions": 4, "total": 17}, "roadmap": {"items": [{"id": "AJCR.w4-rep.datum.dat-j", "title": "DAT-J: JacobianData assembly \u2014 quasi-